zack snyder's army of the dead has  already provided an embarrassment of  riches by the time his third act rolls  around  from zombie tigers to speed ramp  slaughter to tygnotaro rocking a swisher  sweet  and then just when you think there are  no more surprises in store a miracle of  life occurs  or more accurately a miracle of  zombified undeath  army of the dead introduces a fresh take  on the shambling corpses that we all  know and love  namely the movies alpha zombies who are  faster  stronger and more intelligent than their  lesser brothers and sisters  the alphas are the de facto main  antagonists in this new and dead world  with snyder recently describing them as  zombies that have taken another step  suitably then these highly adaptable  creatures are seen getting up to all  kinds of shenanigans  including a few you might not expect  from the ordinary undead  case in point after the beheading of the  alpha's queen her drooly boo  zeus takes her lifeless body somewhere  private  zeus then mournfully roots around in his  beloved's torso with his other zombie  pals close by  presumably for moral support but just  what is that why the old zombie looking  for in the guts of his one and only  why a luminescent blue bundle of undead  fetus of course  which he gently cradles in two cupped  desiccated hands  and well that certainly answers one  question it also raises so many more  here's the big one though where do  zombie babies come from  there's not really a delicate way to put  this but it may have more than a little  bit to do with zombie mommy and zombie  daddy loving each other very much  at least that's what zack snyder had in  mind when he introduced the idea of  zombie children  to his latest movie in a recent  interview with esquire snyder was asked  the big question  how are zombie babies made ever the  detail-oriented director snyder replied  well i believe that some zombie love  happened some sweet zombie lovemaking  then in what can only be described as  the world's fastest retcon he added i  don't know if it was sweet it was  probably  pretty aggressive snyder continued my  theory is that the zombies in our movie  are working toward not needing a human  host to procreate their species if you  will  that's the ultimate evolution and if  that still seems a little vague for your  liking  fear not because esquire's interviewer  knows what we all need to know  when they straighten her past whether  the zombies and army of the dead  like to get busy snyder replied yeah  unfortunately we don't see  that but yes i think theoretically they  do  and just like that movie fans around the  globe found themselves wondering if zack  snyder really knows what the word  unfortunately means but hey there's some  good news here for the walking dead  themselves  after all children are often seen as an  opportunity for new parents to undergo a  little self-reflection  and even become better people maybe the  ability to procreate could afford these  zombies a chance to really think about  what they want from life  maybe they could change their eating  habits or consider finding employment in  a field  that doesn't involve groaning and  chewing on people maybe they can even  learn to love  i don't see nothing wrong with it but i  know that some people would see  something wrong with it but it's my  husband you know  i still love him i've still got the ring  on my finger trisha  probably not though still one thing is  for sure the zombie baby and army of the  dead  isn't actually hollywood's first  go-round with undead infants  however things don't really go smoothly  when a movie chooses to introduce the  spawn of the dead  for example in his pre-hobbit days peter  jackson made the deeply weird  dead alive which featured a truly  disturbing zombie baby  this isn't even the first time that zack  snyder has plugged a zombie baby into  his work  2004's dawn of the dead the director's  feature film debut  also featured a short-lived zombie tyke  but that one doesn't exactly turn out  great either  so what do you think about all this  zombie baby business  maybe we should just chalk this all up  as a failed experiment and let the  zombies get back to eating people's  brains  rather than each other's faces check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about your  favorite movies and tv shows are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

